From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NFC: nxp-nci: do not let one marginal read end the session

Two things make a single transport hiccup permanent on this controller.

An interrupt that arrives before the driver has left cold mode is answered with
-EREMOTEIO, which is then latched into hard_fault. That is not a transport
failure at all: the controller is simply signalling early, and the frame should
be dropped and waited out rather than treated as fatal.

And hard_fault is only cleared on the way into cold mode, so once latched it
survives every subsequent power cycle the core performs. On this handset a
marginal first read leaves the controller healthy but the driver deaf to every
later interrupt.

Drop the early frame instead of faulting, and clear the latch on any mode
change, since a mode change restarts the transport.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
@@ -51,8 +51,13 @@
 	gpiod_set_value(phy->gpiod_en, (mode != NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD) ? 1 : 0);
 	usleep_range(10000, 15000);
 
-	if (mode == NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD)
-		phy->hard_fault = 0;
+	/*
+	 * Any mode change restarts the transport, so a fault latched from a
+	 * previous attempt must not survive it. Clearing this only on the way
+	 * into cold mode left a single marginal read ending the session for
+	 * good, with every later interrupt dropped.
+	 */
+	phy->hard_fault = 0;
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -221,8 +226,12 @@
 		r = nxp_nci_i2c_fw_read(phy, &skb);
 		break;
 	case NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD:
-		r = -EREMOTEIO;
-		break;
+		/*
+		 * The controller can assert its interrupt before the driver
+		 * has left cold mode. That is not a transport failure and
+		 * must not poison the phy: drop the frame and wait.
+		 */
+		goto exit_irq_handled;
 	}
 
 	if (r == -EREMOTEIO) {
--
2.50.1
